  "title": "Stop Seeing Yourself as Complex and Others as Predictable",
  "description": "Stop seeing yourself as complex and others as predictable. Here’s how: - Practice empathy: Imagine how someone else’s day, mood, or challenges might influence their actions. - Ask questions: Get to know others’ perspectives instead of assuming their motives. - Challenge labels: Avoid saying, “They’re always like this,” and consider how context shapes behavior. Example: If a coworker is short with you, consider they might be stressed or distracted instead of labeling them as rude.",
